>
	<p>
		Trango Treks takes its name from the Trango Towers — the sheer granite spires that rise above the
		Baltoro Glacier and stop every trekker in their tracks. We guide small groups through the
		Karakoram of Gilgit-Baltistan, from the classic walk to K2 Base Camp to technical crossings and
		first six-thousanders.
	</p>

	<h2>How we work</h2>
	<p>
		Our trips are built around people who live in these valleys: guides, cooks and porters whose
		knowledge of the glaciers and weather is what makes a journey here safe and memorable. We keep
		groups small, pace every itinerary for acclimatisation and pay our crews fairly.
	</p>

	<blockquote>The mountains are not a backdrop. They are the reason, and they deserve our respect.</blockquote>

	<h2>Travel with us</h2>
	<p>
		Whether you are planning your first high-altitude trek or returning for a summit, we're happy to
		talk through routes, seasons and preparation. <a href="/#plan">Get in touch</a> and we'll help
		you find the right journey.
	</p>
</Layout>
